{"cluster_id": "C-0393", "topic": "CAS blob protocol", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B019-011", "B019-025"], "canonical_claim": "The CA branch of `DataPartStorageOnDiskBase::clonePart` creates one destination transaction, recursively streams every source file through non-autocommit `IDiskTransaction::writeFile`, and commits once. Additionally, The L2 fix copies every part file sequentially through one destination CA transaction and commits once, causing `publishStaging` and `PartWriteTxn` to upload deduplicated blobs, create one manifest, and publish one ref atomically.", "issue_ids": ["S36"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-17-cas-move-to-ca.md#L361-L407", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-17-cas-move-to-ca-design.md#L32-L39"]}
