{"cluster_id": "C-0405", "topic": "CAS blob protocol", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B035-001", "B035-002"], "canonical_claim": "`Build::putBlob` was changed to stream the staged source instead of materializing it in a `String`, resolving the observed CA upload memory blow-up. Additionally, Before the streaming fix, `Build::putBlob` could materialize a `BlobSource` into a `String`, producing about 384 MiB peak RSS for a 64 MiB blob upload; testing this risk requires blobs of at least 256 MiB or the `ci/full` scale.", "issue_ids": ["S01"], "sources": ["utils/ca-soak/scenarios/BACKLOG.md#L25-L44", "utils/ca-soak/scenarios/BACKLOG.md#L305-L318"]}
