{"cluster_id": "C-0416", "topic": "CAS blob protocol", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-015"], "canonical_claim": "The manifest-trust adoption trade-off (D4 relink trust model, ordinary ReplicatedMergeTree interserver trust) means a genuinely-absent adopted blob is no longer caught at promote time \u2014 it becomes an fsck `dangling` finding instead of a promote `ABORTED`; this is verified unreachable in production by source-pin plus durable-edge, backed by an independent EDGE-BEFORE-OBSERVE consult and a per-test reachability proof. This also incidentally fixed the S13 soak-run-3 liveness brick where `republishRef -> promote ABORTED (condemned)` had left a table readonly forever.", "issue_ids": ["S13"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/03-writer-protocol.md#L255-L263"]}
